  "problem": "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=\u27e8-\\sqrt{3},0,-2\u27e9$ and $b\\times c=\u27e8-\\sqrt{3},10,-10\u27e9.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\u27e8-\\sqrt{3},0,-2\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-\\sqrt{3},10,-10\u27e9 \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{3})\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot 10+(-2)\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =3+0+20 \\\\  & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
